1
00:00:28,429 --> 00:00:30,765
Previously on Dating Alys Perez.

2
00:00:32,649 --> 00:00:34,068
Bottoms up!

3
00:00:35,481 --> 00:00:36,607
Tripp's back!

4
00:00:37,191 --> 00:00:37,942
Alys!

5
00:00:38,484 --> 00:00:39,110
Kei?

6
00:00:41,612 --> 00:00:42,363
Alys!

7
00:00:42,530 --> 00:00:44,282
You little witch!

8
00:00:44,307 --> 00:00:45,516
Let's go, Fier.

9
00:00:45,742 --> 00:00:46,993
Have you seen Tripp?

10
00:00:47,660 --> 00:00:48,870
Did you two fight?

11
00:00:49,328 --> 00:00:50,872
We can't be together!

12
00:00:51,372 --> 00:00:53,166
There is no us!
Are you dumb?

13
00:00:53,291 --> 00:00:54,584
Who is Fier?

14
00:00:55,209 --> 00:00:56,586
- Goodbye, Alys.
- Drake!

15
00:00:58,004 --> 00:00:59,380
I thought we were just taking a break.

16
00:01:00,173 --> 00:01:01,924
We never broke up, right?

17
00:01:02,925 --> 00:01:03,885
Okay, Alys.

18
00:01:05,595 --> 00:01:06,512
Let's break up.

19
00:01:07,138 --> 00:01:08,514
I'm setting you free.

20
00:01:09,891 --> 00:01:11,809
So, please let me go, as well.

21
00:01:43,257 --> 00:01:45,176
Good morning, baby!

22
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:47,970
- Good morning, Mommy.
- Come, have a seat.

23
00:01:47,970 --> 00:01:49,388
Let's eat breakfast.

24
00:01:50,431 --> 00:01:51,516
Where's Dad?

25
00:01:51,891 --> 00:01:52,809
Well,

26
00:01:52,809 --> 00:01:54,268
your dad is at work.

27
00:01:54,268 --> 00:01:55,770
And then your little brother

28
00:01:55,770 --> 00:01:57,021
is studying.

29
00:01:57,105 --> 00:01:59,357
So, do you have any plans for today?

30
00:02:00,942 --> 00:02:02,443
Honestly,

31
00:02:02,443 --> 00:02:03,361
I still have a headache

32
00:02:03,361 --> 00:02:06,072
from all the thinking and
pondering I did last night.

33
00:02:07,198 --> 00:02:09,158
Should I do what Tripp says?

34
00:02:10,243 --> 00:02:11,828
Should I chase Drake?

35
00:02:13,412 --> 00:02:14,747
Alys?

36
00:02:14,747 --> 00:02:16,457
Did you stay up all night?

37
00:02:16,666 --> 00:02:18,209
You look sleepy.

38
00:02:20,336 --> 00:02:21,379
Sorry, Mom.

39
00:02:21,379 --> 00:02:23,506
I have a lot going through
my head right now.

40
00:02:24,132 --> 00:02:25,258
Like what?

41
00:02:28,553 --> 00:02:29,554
I'm going on a vacation.

42
00:02:29,804 --> 00:02:31,931
Oh, finally!
Well deserved!

43
00:02:32,056 --> 00:02:33,099
Where are you headed to?

44
00:02:33,641 --> 00:02:34,517
I don't know yet.

45
00:02:35,017 --> 00:02:36,352
Maybe somewhere south.

46
00:02:36,477 --> 00:02:38,104
Oh, good choice!

47
00:02:38,104 --> 00:02:38,771
Okay.

48
00:02:38,771 --> 00:02:39,897
Let's make a deal.

49
00:02:39,897 --> 00:02:41,482
I'll pay for everything, okay?

50
00:02:41,732 --> 00:02:43,234
Just enjoy and relax.

51
00:02:43,442 --> 00:02:44,110
Alright?

52
00:02:44,902 --> 00:02:45,695
Thank you, Mommy.

53
00:02:45,695 --> 00:02:46,946
- You're the best!
- You're welcome!

54
00:02:46,946 --> 00:02:47,905
Okay, let's eat!

55
00:02:48,531 --> 00:02:52,076
I think I really need a vacation
to take my mind off things.

56
00:02:52,577 --> 00:02:55,204
I think I really need this because

57
00:02:55,204 --> 00:02:57,999
lately my mind had been
doing rash things to me.

58
00:03:08,259 --> 00:03:09,427
Hello?

59
00:03:09,927 --> 00:03:12,054
Hi, Bestie!

60
00:03:12,221 --> 00:03:13,514
Aya!

61
00:03:13,514 --> 00:03:15,099
Yes, Bestie, why did you call?

62
00:03:15,099 --> 00:03:15,933
-What’s up?
-Uhm...

63
00:03:16,767 --> 00:03:18,311
Where are you?

64
00:03:18,853 --> 00:03:21,314
Your mom says you're going on a vacation.

65
00:03:21,939 --> 00:03:23,900
Word travels fast!

66
00:03:23,983 --> 00:03:26,152
I'm on the way to Batangas right now.

67
00:03:26,694 --> 00:03:27,653
Why, Bestie?

68
00:03:29,947 --> 00:03:33,201
Have you picked a place to stay?
Any ideas?

69
00:03:33,201 --> 00:03:34,076
Uhm...

70
00:03:34,076 --> 00:03:38,080
At the resort where Mommy usually
books for family vacations.

71
00:03:38,331 --> 00:03:39,874
Why do you ask, Bestie?

72
00:03:40,249 --> 00:03:42,168
Oh! Uhm...
Bestie, nothing.

73
00:03:42,168 --> 00:03:43,461
Okay, uhm...

74
00:03:43,544 --> 00:03:47,215
Enjoy! You deserve it!

75
00:03:48,883 --> 00:03:50,468
Bestie? Bestie!

76
00:03:51,427 --> 00:03:53,638
Hmm? What's Aya’s problem?

77
00:03:53,638 --> 00:03:55,223
It's too early to be hyper.

78
00:03:55,848 --> 00:03:56,682
Oh, well.

79
00:03:56,682 --> 00:03:58,643
I'll just enjoy myself then.

80
00:03:59,894 --> 00:04:01,395
Sun, sand and sea...

81
00:04:01,812 --> 00:04:02,897
Here I come!

82
00:04:14,909 --> 00:04:18,287
There were nights
that I just couldn't sleep.

83
00:04:18,704 --> 00:04:20,623
It felt like torture.

84
00:04:21,082 --> 00:04:24,043
Just lying there,
not being able to sleep at all.

85
00:04:29,215 --> 00:04:30,883
How long should I be gone for?

86
00:04:31,425 --> 00:04:33,386
I think one week should suffice.

87
00:04:33,886 --> 00:04:37,431
After that, my mind should probably be
fresh enough not to screw things up.

88
00:04:38,140 --> 00:04:40,101
I'll follow Tripp's advice.

89
00:04:41,018 --> 00:04:44,021
Maybe I'll try to fix
things up with Drake.

90
00:04:44,939 --> 00:04:47,233
No, not chase him back.

91
00:04:47,650 --> 00:04:50,152
I just want to have
things back to normal.

92
00:06:54,693 --> 00:06:56,987
Maybe Tripp was right.

93
00:06:56,987 --> 00:06:59,281
I still love Drake.

94
00:06:59,532 --> 00:07:01,826
I think I never stopped loving him.

95
00:07:02,785 --> 00:07:05,079
He was my epic love.

96
00:07:05,621 --> 00:07:07,081
But,

97
00:07:07,081 --> 00:07:08,874
I don't want that kind of love.

98
00:07:09,834 --> 00:07:11,836
I just want a quiet life.

99
00:07:12,545 --> 00:07:15,131
Complications would never be my thing.

100
00:07:31,564 --> 00:07:33,482
Hello, Ma'am.
Good morning.

101
00:07:33,482 --> 00:07:35,651
Good morning, Sir.

102
00:08:13,856 --> 00:08:15,357
Good morning, Ms. Perez.

103
00:08:15,357 --> 00:08:16,817
Hi!

104
00:08:16,817 --> 00:08:18,402
A welcome drink, Ma'am?

105
00:08:18,402 --> 00:08:19,570
No, thanks.

106
00:08:22,990 --> 00:08:24,158
Why is she calling?

107
00:08:24,742 --> 00:08:25,910
Maybe she felt guilty?

108
00:08:27,119 --> 00:08:28,454
But why would she?

109
00:08:28,454 --> 00:08:29,788
It wasn't like...

110
00:08:30,331 --> 00:08:32,208
Sorry, Kei.
Vacation mode.

111
00:08:32,291 --> 00:08:34,168
On a vacation.

112
00:08:34,168 --> 00:08:36,253
Look after Tripp for me, okay?

113
00:08:36,253 --> 00:08:38,130
Thanks, Kei. XOXO

114
00:08:38,130 --> 00:08:41,592
Hi, Ma'am!
Welcome to Layag Resort!

115
00:08:41,592 --> 00:08:42,384
Hello!

116
00:08:42,384 --> 00:08:43,427
How may I help you today?

117
00:08:43,427 --> 00:08:45,846
I have a reservation under Alys Perez.

118
00:08:45,930 --> 00:08:47,598
Alys Perez.

119
00:08:47,598 --> 00:08:49,016
Okay, thank you Ma'am.

120
00:08:49,016 --> 00:08:51,852
Hold on, I'll just check the
details on the reservation.

121
00:08:57,983 --> 00:09:00,753
Ma'am, here's your key!

122
00:09:00,785 --> 00:09:01,708
- Thank —
- Ah!

123
00:09:01,987 --> 00:09:03,072
By the way, Ma'am,

124
00:09:03,072 --> 00:09:06,909
we have accomodated the changes
made to the booking earlier.

125
00:09:07,660 --> 00:09:08,827
Changes?

126
00:09:08,827 --> 00:09:10,204
Yes, Ma'am. Changes.

127
00:09:10,204 --> 00:09:13,859
Actually, someone called earlier
to upgrade your room from

128
00:09:13,884 --> 00:09:16,887
lower villa to upper villa!

129
00:09:17,001 --> 00:09:18,169
For a better view.

130
00:09:18,504 --> 00:09:20,631
Huh? I'm sorry?

131
00:09:21,090 --> 00:09:22,341
Actually, Ma'am,

132
00:09:22,341 --> 00:09:26,053
the same card was used for
the adjustment of your room, yes.

133
00:09:26,303 --> 00:09:28,180
Oh yeah, that's Mom's card.

134
00:09:28,305 --> 00:09:30,057
She must've upgraded my room!

135
00:09:30,057 --> 00:09:34,144
Oh, that's so sweet of her!
She really knows I need this vacation.

136
00:09:34,362 --> 00:09:35,811
Okay, thank you.

137
00:09:36,146 --> 00:09:39,149
If you're ready and
everything is settled then,

138
00:09:39,525 --> 00:09:41,569
we will escort you to your room.

139
00:09:42,027 --> 00:09:42,998
Okay.

140
00:09:43,279 --> 00:09:44,264
Just hold on.

141
00:09:48,033 --> 00:09:48,975
Drake?!

142
00:09:50,119 --> 00:09:51,287
What is Drake doing here?!

143
00:09:55,666 --> 00:09:56,750
Oh my god!

144
00:10:04,457 --> 00:10:05,667
Good morning, sir.

145
00:10:05,718 --> 00:10:06,552
Good morning.

146
00:10:07,094 --> 00:10:08,345
Here’s your welcome drink.

147
00:10:08,345 --> 00:10:09,555
Thank you.

148
00:10:24,903 --> 00:10:25,738
Hello, Mommy?

149
00:10:25,738 --> 00:10:27,490
Hi, Bestie!

150
00:10:27,698 --> 00:10:28,584
Aya?!

151
00:10:29,074 --> 00:10:30,242
Yes, Bestie!

152
00:10:30,242 --> 00:10:32,328
The one and only.

153
00:10:32,703 --> 00:10:34,038
Why do you have Mommy's phone?

154
00:10:36,665 --> 00:10:38,876
She says she doesn't
want to talk to you.

155
00:10:39,225 --> 00:10:40,836
How come?

156
00:10:41,128 --> 00:10:44,982
Do you know why my room
upgraded to an upper villa?

157
00:10:45,007 --> 00:10:47,176
And do you have an idea
why Drake is here?

158
00:10:47,384 --> 00:10:49,219
Don't you remember, Bestie?

159
00:10:49,219 --> 00:10:52,973
I'm #TeamDralys for life.

160
00:10:53,182 --> 00:10:54,451
You're both grownups.

161
00:10:54,642 --> 00:10:57,436
Make love, not war.

162
00:10:57,686 --> 00:11:00,898
Oh my god, Aya! What the hell?!

163
00:11:01,482 --> 00:11:02,990
Just stay there.

164
00:11:03,108 --> 00:11:04,818
Don't be such a killjoy, okay?

165
00:11:05,277 --> 00:11:08,030
Damn it, Aya. You're so crazy!

166
00:11:08,131 --> 00:11:10,049
What are you trying to pull now, huh?

167
00:11:10,074 --> 00:11:11,283
No, Bestie,

168
00:11:11,575 --> 00:11:12,910
I'm not crazy.

169
00:11:12,910 --> 00:11:14,662
I'm your best friend, okay?

170
00:11:14,870 --> 00:11:16,662
So sit back and relax.

171
00:11:16,914 --> 00:11:19,875
And if nothing happens over the week,

172
00:11:19,875 --> 00:11:22,795
I shall never talk about Drake

173
00:11:22,795 --> 00:11:25,089
ever again.

174
00:11:25,089 --> 00:11:26,382
Promise.

175
00:11:26,382 --> 00:11:28,509
Even if it'll hurt my heart.

176
00:11:28,717 --> 00:11:32,930
I'll shift to #TeamTrippZy instead.

177
00:11:32,930 --> 00:11:36,642
Damn it, Aya. You're insane!

178
00:11:37,309 --> 00:11:38,769
You're welcome, Bestie.

179
00:11:38,936 --> 00:11:41,563
Love you. Enjoy!

180
00:11:41,563 --> 00:11:45,395
Make love, not war.

181
00:11:46,068 --> 00:11:47,661
Hello? Hello!

182
00:11:50,280 --> 00:11:52,241
Aya, that little witch!

183
00:11:53,367 --> 00:11:56,286
What's her deal?
Why is she so into this kind of thrill?

184
00:11:57,121 --> 00:11:58,539
Okay, Alys.

185
00:11:58,539 --> 00:12:02,501
In yoga, they tell you to
take three deep breaths.

186
00:12:10,467 --> 00:12:12,511
Okay, Alys. Aja!

187
00:12:21,353 --> 00:12:22,563
Hi!

188
00:12:23,564 --> 00:12:24,289
Hi?

189
00:12:24,314 --> 00:12:25,274
What are you doing here?

190
00:12:26,552 --> 00:12:27,512
Dad.

191
00:12:28,026 --> 00:12:31,321
Gosh, he's back to his
one-word utterances.

192
00:12:32,030 --> 00:12:33,657
So Drake Palma.

193
00:12:34,700 --> 00:12:37,703
Excuse me, can I change rooms?

194
00:12:37,703 --> 00:12:41,415
The upper villas are too big for me.

195
00:12:43,250 --> 00:12:45,919
Actually, Ma'am, all rooms are occupied.

196
00:12:45,919 --> 00:12:47,254
I’m sorry.

197
00:12:49,590 --> 00:12:50,808
Seriously?

198
00:12:54,428 --> 00:12:56,680
I don't see any other guests here.

199
00:12:57,389 --> 00:12:58,390
Uh...

200
00:12:58,932 --> 00:13:03,312
Actually, Ma’am, all rooms are paid for
under the name of Ms...

201
00:13:03,353 --> 00:13:05,189
Dana Guzman.

202
00:13:06,106 --> 00:13:07,733
Shit, Aya.

203
00:13:08,901 --> 00:13:13,753
I understand but my mom's
not even here so...

204
00:13:14,815 --> 00:13:18,861
Yes, Ma'am. But unfortunately,
we cannot change the booking.

205
00:13:19,203 --> 00:13:23,123
Because the rooms are paid
for under a different name.

206
00:13:23,704 --> 00:13:26,226
But, the good thing is

207
00:13:26,251 --> 00:13:30,214
the upper villa is still
available for the two of you!

208
00:13:31,048 --> 00:13:32,341
Perfect.

209
00:13:36,553 --> 00:13:37,596
Take the room.

210
00:13:38,639 --> 00:13:39,620
I’ll just leave.

211
00:13:41,725 --> 00:13:44,019
Me too. I'm not in the mood
for a vacation anymore.

212
00:13:53,028 --> 00:13:54,571
Aya!

213
00:14:02,204 --> 00:14:03,914
And what are you smiling about?

214
00:14:04,414 --> 00:14:05,332
Nothing.

215
00:14:10,212 --> 00:14:11,081
Fine!

216
00:14:13,507 --> 00:14:15,551
Okay, Ma'am. Have a nice day!

217
00:14:15,551 --> 00:14:17,261
Enjoy your stay!

218
00:14:17,261 --> 00:14:20,013
Love, love, love!

219
00:14:20,430 --> 00:14:21,253
Tss.

220
00:14:21,431 --> 00:14:24,784
My phone is useless. My car is useless.

221
00:14:29,439 --> 00:14:30,774
Share a room?

222
00:14:44,872 --> 00:14:48,792
As you can see, the resort
has plenty of space!

223
00:14:48,792 --> 00:14:51,336
This place is a perfect place.

224
00:14:51,587 --> 00:14:54,381
To relax, enjoy...

225
00:14:54,381 --> 00:14:56,508
and be in love!

226
00:14:57,467 --> 00:14:59,136
With the nature, of course.

227
00:14:59,303 --> 00:15:02,472
On the left side is the tranquil sea,

228
00:15:02,472 --> 00:15:03,849
with it's wide shore

229
00:15:04,141 --> 00:15:06,810
where you can chase
each other's feelings.

230
00:15:06,810 --> 00:15:09,479
I mean, you two could chase
each other along the shore.

231
00:15:10,022 --> 00:15:12,941
This place is magical!

232
00:15:12,941 --> 00:15:14,401
Like you two.

233
00:15:16,028 --> 00:15:17,404
Ahh!

234
00:15:17,404 --> 00:15:18,906
Finally!

235
00:15:18,906 --> 00:15:21,491
This is your villa!

236
00:15:21,491 --> 00:15:27,164
As mentioned earlier, the two of
you will stay on the upper villa.

237
00:15:27,164 --> 00:15:32,252
For a romantic, intimate
and better view.

238
00:15:32,277 --> 00:15:37,507
So, follow me and
I'm sure you'll love this.

239
00:15:37,507 --> 00:15:39,760
I'm so excited for your stay here.

240
00:15:39,760 --> 00:15:41,762
And look at the view!

241
00:15:41,845 --> 00:15:44,097
You can see the vast ocean.

242
00:15:44,222 --> 00:15:46,683
You can hang out there at night.

243
00:15:48,060 --> 00:15:50,354
Follow me.
Okay guys, just follow me.

244
00:15:50,354 --> 00:15:52,773
Be careful with the luggages.

245
00:15:55,233 --> 00:15:56,944
Let's go!

246
00:15:56,944 --> 00:15:59,696
Ms. Perez and Mr. Palma,

247
00:15:59,696 --> 00:16:03,659
this is your beautiful
and intimate villa!

248
00:16:08,538 --> 00:16:11,875
Are you sure that there aren't
any other villas available?

249
00:16:12,584 --> 00:16:13,418
Yes, Ma'am.

250
00:16:13,418 --> 00:16:16,213
Like I said, we're fully booked
right now.

251
00:16:16,213 --> 00:16:17,589
This the only one available.

252
00:16:17,756 --> 00:16:18,382
Fully booked?

253
00:16:18,382 --> 00:16:20,092
But it was my mom
who booked the rooms.

254
00:16:20,092 --> 00:16:22,260
And you don't have
any other guests here.

255
00:16:24,680 --> 00:16:27,975
This is the only available
villa and room, Ma'am.

256
00:16:27,975 --> 00:16:29,309
It's nice here!

257
00:16:29,954 --> 00:16:30,727
Okay.

258
00:16:32,104 --> 00:16:33,647
I guess this is my room.

259
00:16:33,647 --> 00:16:36,108
Ma'am, sorry.
This room is not available.

260
00:16:36,108 --> 00:16:37,317
The keys for the lock are missing.

261
00:16:37,609 --> 00:16:39,736
- Are you sure?
- Uh, yes, Ma'am.

262
00:16:39,736 --> 00:16:40,988
Ms. Perez,

263
00:16:41,154 --> 00:16:42,114
Mr. Palma,

264
00:16:42,114 --> 00:16:43,031
follow me.

265
00:16:43,031 --> 00:16:43,782
Follow me.

266
00:16:47,244 --> 00:16:50,095
This is your beautiful room.

267
00:16:53,041 --> 00:16:55,704
This room comes with air condition,

268
00:16:56,020 --> 00:16:58,815
a flatscreen TV and free WiFi.

269
00:16:59,214 --> 00:17:01,800
And through that door is the bathroom

270
00:17:02,092 --> 00:17:04,469
where basic toiletries are provided

271
00:17:04,469 --> 00:17:06,138
and fresh towels.

272
00:17:07,556 --> 00:17:08,974
Not only that,

273
00:17:09,683 --> 00:17:11,893
the best thing about this room is...

274
00:17:13,061 --> 00:17:15,981
is the best view of the beach.

275
00:17:16,273 --> 00:17:19,026
It's so romantic!

276
00:17:19,568 --> 00:17:21,903
Makes you fall in love, right?

277
00:17:22,446 --> 00:17:24,823
So, Ms. Perez,

278
00:17:25,157 --> 00:17:27,367
Mr. Palma, I'll go ahead.

279
00:17:27,492 --> 00:17:30,954
Again...
Love, love, love!

280
00:17:31,371 --> 00:17:33,373
Enjoy your stay!

281
00:17:33,795 --> 00:17:36,548
I am so going to kill you, Aya!

282
00:17:38,086 --> 00:17:40,547
One room, one bed?

283
00:17:42,340 --> 00:17:43,425
You take the bed.

284
00:17:56,813 --> 00:17:57,634
Drake.

285
00:17:59,316 --> 00:18:01,777
I know you're not comfortable
sleeping on the couch.

286
00:18:01,902 --> 00:18:03,361
You’re like a prince in your home.

287
00:18:03,361 --> 00:18:04,863
Uncle Steve doesn’t even
make you do anything,

288
00:18:04,863 --> 00:18:06,531
and you expect me to
let you sleep there?

289
00:18:07,449 --> 00:18:08,321
So, what?

290
00:18:08,784 --> 00:18:11,328
You expect me to let you sleep here?

291
00:18:14,164 --> 00:18:14,956
Uhm...

292
00:18:16,376 --> 00:18:17,400
Uhm...

293
00:18:20,712 --> 00:18:21,838
We can...

294
00:18:23,590 --> 00:18:24,382
We can share a bed —

295
00:18:24,382 --> 00:18:25,008
No!

296
00:18:26,343 --> 00:18:27,319
No, but —

297
00:18:27,344 --> 00:18:28,228
Alys!

298
00:18:29,971 --> 00:18:30,847
I'm a man.

299
00:18:32,099 --> 00:18:33,433
And I'm still

300
00:18:33,433 --> 00:18:34,768
in love with you.

301
00:18:35,602 --> 00:18:36,812
So don't dare me.

302
00:18:42,150 --> 00:18:43,568
Can I use your bathroom?

303
00:18:43,568 --> 00:18:44,486
I’ll just have a quick shower.

304
00:18:46,571 --> 00:18:47,280
Hmm.

305
00:18:49,199 --> 00:18:50,181
Thank you.

306
00:19:12,305 --> 00:19:15,725
It's better for him to stay
here instead of the couch.

307
00:19:15,725 --> 00:19:17,644
It's more comfortable here.

308
00:19:19,896 --> 00:19:21,439
He’s taking so long to take a bath.

309
00:19:23,525 --> 00:19:24,234
Oh no.

310
00:19:24,317 --> 00:19:26,945
I might see his body
when he comes out after showering.

311
00:19:26,945 --> 00:19:28,446
I need a distraction.

312
00:19:36,496 --> 00:19:37,414
Ahh!

313
00:19:37,873 --> 00:19:39,749
Oh my god!

314
00:19:43,628 --> 00:19:46,715
Why are they all adult channels?

315
00:19:47,382 --> 00:19:48,675
- What?
- Oh, god!

316
00:19:50,093 --> 00:19:50,552
Oh my god!

317
00:19:50,552 --> 00:19:52,220
Oh my god!

318
00:19:52,470 --> 00:19:53,972
Don't startle me, Alys!

319
00:19:54,274 --> 00:19:55,441
You’re the one who startled me!

320
00:19:55,473 --> 00:19:57,559
You didn’t say you were finished
taking a shower!

321
00:19:58,018 --> 00:19:59,686
Oh, yeah.

322
00:19:59,686 --> 00:20:00,687
It's your turn.

323
00:20:01,229 --> 00:20:02,189
Okay.

324
00:20:02,606 --> 00:20:03,815
Are you done?

325
00:20:04,316 --> 00:20:05,358
I'm done.

326
00:20:05,442 --> 00:20:06,359
Are you sure?

327
00:20:09,196 --> 00:20:10,030
Okay.

328
00:20:28,632 --> 00:20:31,176
It seems nice to take a
walk along the shore.

329
00:20:51,529 --> 00:20:53,323
How did we end up like this?

330
00:20:53,698 --> 00:20:56,117
We used to be so comfortable
around each other.

331
00:20:56,576 --> 00:20:59,329
To the point where I was even
able to touch his underwear.

332
00:21:00,413 --> 00:21:01,556
But now,

333
00:21:01,831 --> 00:21:04,376
I can't even look him in the eye.

334
00:21:05,001 --> 00:21:06,503
Funny how things work, right?

335
00:21:21,726 --> 00:21:22,602
Alys.

336
00:21:25,397 --> 00:21:27,107
Drake, uhm...

337
00:21:31,820 --> 00:21:33,571
Alys, would you...

338
00:21:38,315 --> 00:21:39,399
Huh?

339
00:21:40,370 --> 00:21:41,454
Would you

340
00:21:42,789 --> 00:21:45,083
treat me the same way
you did before?

341
00:21:47,777 --> 00:21:50,964
You've been acting so cringe lately.

342
00:21:55,343 --> 00:21:56,344
Sure.

343
00:21:57,012 --> 00:21:58,513
He really did love me.

344
00:21:59,347 --> 00:22:00,473
I hope...

345
00:22:00,473 --> 00:22:02,976
I hope he finds someone he can love.

346
00:22:03,768 --> 00:22:04,811
Not me but,

347
00:22:04,811 --> 00:22:06,271
someone who's worthy of him.

348
00:22:06,855 --> 00:22:08,231
Drake is a fine man.

349
00:22:08,231 --> 00:22:10,191
Any girl would be lucky to have him.

350
00:22:12,152 --> 00:22:13,320
Uh...

351
00:22:14,487 --> 00:22:16,281
Do you want to go for a walk?

352
00:22:31,046 --> 00:22:32,047
Drake!

353
00:22:32,297 --> 00:22:33,381
Drake!

354
00:22:39,971 --> 00:22:41,848
Hey, Drake, wait for me!

355
00:22:42,974 --> 00:22:43,885
Hey!

356
00:22:46,561 --> 00:22:48,730
Drake, wait for me.

357
00:22:50,637 --> 00:22:51,763
Oh, geez!

358
00:23:10,585 --> 00:23:11,920
Why are you laughing?

359
00:23:12,712 --> 00:23:13,755
Was that funny?

360
00:23:16,925 --> 00:23:17,967
This.

361
00:23:19,427 --> 00:23:20,470
Us.

362
00:23:22,347 --> 00:23:24,391
It's like we're in high school

363
00:23:24,391 --> 00:23:25,975
all over again.

364
00:23:26,893 --> 00:23:28,186
Huh?

365
00:23:29,187 --> 00:23:30,105
Alys?

366
00:23:30,480 --> 00:23:31,272
Hmm?

367
00:23:33,271 --> 00:23:37,416
Can we go back to how
we were in high school?

368
00:23:38,836 --> 00:23:39,837
But...

369
00:23:39,862 --> 00:23:40,863
It’s because —

370
00:23:42,742 --> 00:23:44,994
High school is my fondest memory.

371
00:23:46,621 --> 00:23:48,081
Because in high school,

372
00:23:48,651 --> 00:23:49,861
I had you.

373
00:23:54,754 --> 00:23:55,713
But —

374
00:23:55,713 --> 00:23:57,215
So on this day

375
00:23:58,216 --> 00:24:01,511
and the next few days
that we’ll be here at this resort,

376
00:24:04,556 --> 00:24:07,684
can we go back to how things
were in high school?

377
00:24:08,726 --> 00:24:12,188
Can you make me feel like
we're back in high school again?

378
00:24:13,314 --> 00:24:16,192
After that, you can go back
to your reality, Alys.

379
00:24:16,734 --> 00:24:18,361
What about your reality?

380
00:24:18,778 --> 00:24:20,530
My reality sucks.

381
00:24:21,489 --> 00:24:22,782
How come?

382
00:24:22,782 --> 00:24:24,242
You have Cristine.

383
00:24:24,868 --> 00:24:26,327
And... Fier.

384
00:24:29,122 --> 00:24:29,956
What do you mean?

385
00:24:30,582 --> 00:24:31,416
I mean...

386
00:24:33,626 --> 00:24:34,794
Nothing.

387
00:24:34,794 --> 00:24:35,587
Never mind.

388
00:24:35,837 --> 00:24:38,798
Alys, don't force it
if you can't say it.

389
00:24:42,802 --> 00:24:43,553
Huh?

390
00:24:57,540 --> 00:24:59,029
My reality sucks.

391
00:25:00,195 --> 00:25:02,029
Because you're no longer with me.

392
00:25:05,283 --> 00:25:06,388
So, Alys...

393
00:25:06,910 --> 00:25:09,412
Can you give me this one vacation?

394
00:25:16,628 --> 00:25:17,779
But, Tripp...

395
00:25:18,588 --> 00:25:20,673
I really did care about Tripp.

396
00:25:20,673 --> 00:25:22,509
Unlike what he believed in,

397
00:25:22,509 --> 00:25:24,511
he was my priority.

398
00:25:24,511 --> 00:25:27,013
I think about him
before I make decisions.

399
00:25:27,430 --> 00:25:29,265
Well, most of the time.

400
00:25:29,641 --> 00:25:31,059
Just one week.

401
00:25:33,937 --> 00:25:35,772
Wouldn't that be selfish?

402
00:25:36,397 --> 00:25:37,524
Selfish?

403
00:25:40,610 --> 00:25:42,325
All my life, Alys,

404
00:25:42,612 --> 00:25:44,155
I've been the one giving.

405
00:25:44,906 --> 00:25:46,199
Making sacrifices.

406
00:25:47,492 --> 00:25:50,245
Can I be selfish just this once?

407
00:25:51,246 --> 00:25:52,789
I don't know what to say anymore.

408
00:25:53,729 --> 00:25:56,107
This is Drake Palma talking to me.

409
00:25:56,751 --> 00:25:59,128
And he is practically begging.

410
00:25:59,754 --> 00:26:03,132
Who am I to refuse
what he’s asking for?

411
00:26:07,679 --> 00:26:08,606
Drake?

412
00:26:09,681 --> 00:26:10,557
What?

413
00:26:15,603 --> 00:26:18,731
I'll be your fairy godmother.

414
00:26:19,357 --> 00:26:23,653
And we'll go back to the time
when we first met!

415
00:26:24,988 --> 00:26:25,863
Boom!

416
00:26:25,863 --> 00:26:27,699
We're back in SCA!

417
00:26:30,451 --> 00:26:31,911
Hi, Drakey Baby!

418
00:26:33,204 --> 00:26:34,832
God, he smiled!

419
00:26:35,123 --> 00:26:37,041
And not a little, forced smile, okay.

420
00:26:37,041 --> 00:26:38,960
He freaking smiled!

421
00:26:40,628 --> 00:26:43,548
Bird brain! Always a noob.

422
00:26:44,841 --> 00:26:47,176
You're a meanie. Such a meanie!

423
00:26:51,120 --> 00:26:52,205
Let’s go on a date.

424
00:26:52,230 --> 00:26:53,481
Only if you’re treating me.

425
00:26:57,145 --> 00:26:58,896
This beach is beautiful.

426
00:26:59,897 --> 00:27:01,691
I missed you so much.

427
00:27:02,025 --> 00:27:04,277
Me too, Drakey Baby.

428
00:27:37,268 --> 00:27:38,019
Ahh!

429
00:27:41,189 --> 00:27:42,565
What happened?

430
00:27:45,443 --> 00:27:47,654
Oh my god!
That's a lot of blood.

431
00:27:53,826 --> 00:27:54,577
Hey!

432
00:27:54,577 --> 00:27:56,037
What happened to you?

433
00:27:59,374 --> 00:28:00,210
Geez.

434
00:28:01,459 --> 00:28:03,002
Relax, it's just a cut.

435
00:28:03,034 --> 00:28:06,204
Seeing blood just makes me nauseous.

436
00:28:06,339 --> 00:28:09,384
My classmate in Paris,
he cut his finger.

437
00:28:09,763 --> 00:28:11,807
And now, everytime I see blood

438
00:28:11,886 --> 00:28:12,887
I throw up.

439
00:28:15,932 --> 00:28:17,183
It's okay, Alys.

440
00:28:19,686 --> 00:28:22,063
Even if it's bloody, just don't look.

441
00:28:27,694 --> 00:28:28,903
Are you okay now?

442
00:28:34,659 --> 00:28:35,827
Drake?

443
00:28:36,244 --> 00:28:37,537
What's his problem?

444
00:28:38,538 --> 00:28:39,497
Hey, Drake!

445
00:28:39,497 --> 00:28:41,040
What's your problem?

446
00:28:41,040 --> 00:28:42,583
I thought we were all good?

447
00:28:42,583 --> 00:28:43,793
I thought we had a truce?

448
00:28:43,793 --> 00:28:44,752
A ceasefire?

449
00:28:44,752 --> 00:28:45,837
What is it now?

450
00:28:46,129 --> 00:28:47,547
Hey, Drake!
Are you really not going to answer —

451
00:28:47,547 --> 00:28:48,423
Are you pregnant?

452
00:28:50,216 --> 00:28:50,984
Huh?

453
00:28:52,051 --> 00:28:53,015
What?

454
00:28:55,645 --> 00:28:56,896
What the hell, Drake?

455
00:28:57,464 --> 00:29:00,217
You're going to ask me that
and then turn your back on me?

456
00:29:01,102 --> 00:29:02,437
Are you crazy?

457
00:29:03,153 --> 00:29:06,406
Listen, Drake Sebastian
Jimenez Palma.

458
00:29:08,109 --> 00:29:08,929
What?

459
00:29:10,862 --> 00:29:12,697
So what if I am pregnant?

460
00:29:13,968 --> 00:29:17,201
Don't ask me a question if you're
not ready for the answer.

461
00:29:18,119 --> 00:29:20,121
I feel like I'm challenging the devil.

462
00:29:20,246 --> 00:29:22,790
The thrill is enveloping my very soul.

463
00:29:22,999 --> 00:29:25,209
It's like playing with fire.

464
00:29:25,293 --> 00:29:27,628
Something you know is dangerous,
yet you still want it.

465
00:29:30,214 --> 00:29:33,009
I don't care who
that child's father is

466
00:29:33,009 --> 00:29:35,011
as long as you're the mother.

467
00:29:36,758 --> 00:29:39,428
I've stopped caring
about everything, Alys.

468
00:29:39,916 --> 00:29:41,585
I only care about you.

469
00:29:41,726 --> 00:29:43,394
You're the only one I want.

470
00:29:43,394 --> 00:29:45,938
And everything else is just a bonus.

471
00:29:48,594 --> 00:29:49,632
Drake...

472
00:29:51,751 --> 00:29:52,501
So?

473
00:29:53,738 --> 00:29:54,679
You're really pregnant.

474
00:29:57,116 --> 00:29:57,909
I’m not.

475
00:30:00,828 --> 00:30:01,554
Drake...

476
00:30:02,371 --> 00:30:04,373
Living abroad for five years?

477
00:30:05,500 --> 00:30:07,460
Sleeping around has
always been an option.

478
00:30:07,794 --> 00:30:09,545
All my classmates did it but

479
00:30:09,921 --> 00:30:11,589
that's just really not me.

480
00:30:14,126 --> 00:30:15,502
Thank you.

481
00:30:17,428 --> 00:30:19,263
Why? For what?

482
00:30:21,832 --> 00:30:22,666
For this.

483
00:30:24,936 --> 00:30:25,789
This.

484
00:30:26,515 --> 00:30:27,438
And this.

485
00:30:30,066 --> 00:30:32,443
You're so sappy,
it's getting annoying!

486
00:30:32,965 --> 00:30:34,509
That's not you.

487
00:30:34,862 --> 00:30:36,322
Let's go. It's getting late.

488
00:30:38,241 --> 00:30:39,617
You're so sappy!

489
00:30:43,329 --> 00:30:45,498
Drakey Baby, I’m hungry.

490
00:30:50,586 --> 00:30:53,506
It’s really quiet here
at the resort, isn’t it?

491
00:30:56,107 --> 00:30:59,485
You can’t see anything,
but I can hear something, Alys.

492
00:31:00,513 --> 00:31:01,472
Huh?

493
00:31:02,125 --> 00:31:03,391
Hearing what?

494
00:31:04,767 --> 00:31:07,103
I don't hear anything but the waves.

495
00:31:07,311 --> 00:31:08,396
Shh!

496
00:31:09,230 --> 00:31:11,315
There are voices.
Can’t you hear them?

497
00:31:13,568 --> 00:31:14,944
Voices?

498
00:31:15,528 --> 00:31:17,363
Damn it, Drake!

499
00:31:17,989 --> 00:31:20,408
I can't hear anything!
What voices?

500
00:31:21,939 --> 00:31:24,178
That's it.
I'm calling mom and Aya.

501
00:31:24,203 --> 00:31:26,122
Why would they book me here?

502
00:31:26,122 --> 00:31:27,039
- Ahh!
- Ahh!

503
00:31:27,039 --> 00:31:28,291
Oh my god!

504
00:31:28,708 --> 00:31:29,917
You're such a noob!

505
00:31:30,042 --> 00:31:31,919
Argh!
You're such an idiot!

506
00:31:31,919 --> 00:31:33,796
Why are you scaring me?

507
00:31:34,505 --> 00:31:36,591
Don't scare me like that.

508
00:31:36,591 --> 00:31:38,342
Give that to me!
I don't know what to do with you.

509
00:31:38,342 --> 00:31:39,385
I'm ordering food.

510
00:31:39,385 --> 00:31:40,011
Get it yourself.

511
00:31:40,011 --> 00:31:41,012
I'm ordering food!

512
00:31:41,012 --> 00:31:41,512
Go get it.

513
00:31:41,512 --> 00:31:43,055
Come on!

514
00:31:49,477 --> 00:31:51,104
There’s no wifi.

515
00:31:52,607 --> 00:31:54,025
I’ll just call instead.

516
00:31:59,554 --> 00:32:01,574
We’re sorry.
Your call cannot be completed.

517
00:32:01,574 --> 00:32:03,034
There's no reception.

518
00:32:04,702 --> 00:32:06,329
I’ll just go down.

519
00:32:12,251 --> 00:32:13,252
Never mind.

520
00:32:14,253 --> 00:32:15,713
I don’t want to go down alone.

521
00:32:15,713 --> 00:32:17,506
I might end up seeing something else.

522
00:32:20,718 --> 00:32:22,720
I thought you were hungry?

523
00:32:23,512 --> 00:32:24,722
I'm fine.

524
00:32:25,473 --> 00:32:27,099
I'll sleep it off.

525
00:32:27,266 --> 00:32:28,559
My feet hurt.

526
00:32:28,935 --> 00:32:31,103
We walked a long way earlier.

527
00:32:38,694 --> 00:32:39,654
What are you doing?

528
00:32:39,654 --> 00:32:40,571
Sit.

529
00:32:47,244 --> 00:32:48,162
You know,

530
00:32:49,080 --> 00:32:52,583
you've always had weak legs
since high school.

531
00:33:15,189 --> 00:33:16,098
Better?

532
00:33:44,885 --> 00:33:45,970
Noob.

533
00:33:46,846 --> 00:33:48,180
Hmm?

534
00:33:48,704 --> 00:33:50,099
Noob.

535
00:33:50,640 --> 00:33:52,016
What?

536
00:33:52,041 --> 00:33:54,877
Please let me sleep. I'm so tired.

537
00:33:55,646 --> 00:33:56,605
Noob.

538
00:33:57,565 --> 00:33:58,983
Drake, please, I'm sorry.

539
00:33:58,983 --> 00:34:02,611
My sleepiness is winning
over you right now.

540
00:34:02,778 --> 00:34:03,529
Please.

541
00:34:03,529 --> 00:34:04,405
Let's eat.

542
00:34:07,033 --> 00:34:08,284
Let's go eat.

543
00:34:10,077 --> 00:34:11,287
Get up.

544
00:34:12,038 --> 00:34:13,372
You're getting up.

545
00:34:14,081 --> 00:34:16,083
You're getting up.

546
00:34:17,501 --> 00:34:18,544
Eat.

547
00:34:23,049 --> 00:34:24,592
What's all this?

548
00:34:24,675 --> 00:34:25,533
Food.

549
00:34:29,204 --> 00:34:31,165
I know it's food, Drake.

550
00:34:31,307 --> 00:34:33,517
But why is there so much?

551
00:34:46,530 --> 00:34:47,751
Alys,

552
00:34:48,032 --> 00:34:50,534
I'm not letting you go hungry.

553
00:34:51,035 --> 00:34:51,869
There.

554
00:34:52,286 --> 00:34:53,788
Make yourself happy.

555
00:34:56,123 --> 00:34:57,208
What do you want?

556
00:34:57,708 --> 00:34:58,834
Surprise me.

557
00:35:01,378 --> 00:35:02,797
I know this one's your favorite.

558
00:35:16,227 --> 00:35:17,103
Oh!

559
00:35:19,980 --> 00:35:22,108
Wait, that's too much!

560
00:35:23,317 --> 00:35:24,735
You need to get fat.

561
00:35:25,903 --> 00:35:26,904
I don't want to!

562
00:35:28,572 --> 00:35:29,501
Why?

563
00:35:29,698 --> 00:35:32,034
I worked hard for this
figure, you know?

564
00:35:33,869 --> 00:35:35,412
You look like a stick.

565
00:35:35,913 --> 00:35:36,831
Huh?!

566
00:35:39,041 --> 00:35:41,502
I could draw you right
now using stick figures.

567
00:35:42,211 --> 00:35:43,462
You're mean.

568
00:35:44,380 --> 00:35:45,965
You're a bad person, Drake.

569
00:35:52,054 --> 00:35:53,180
Drink.

570
00:36:06,819 --> 00:36:08,070
Stop staring.

571
00:36:08,988 --> 00:36:10,406
I can't help it.

572
00:36:12,908 --> 00:36:14,743
Seriously, Sebastian?

573
00:36:15,035 --> 00:36:16,245
I'm not going anywhere!

574
00:36:16,662 --> 00:36:19,623
I can't eat when you
stare at me like that.

575
00:36:20,666 --> 00:36:22,751
I won't run away. So, chill!

576
00:36:22,751 --> 00:36:24,253
You should eat too.

577
00:36:25,880 --> 00:36:27,956
You always say that you won't.

578
00:36:28,299 --> 00:36:31,302
But I always find myself chasing you.

579
00:36:35,014 --> 00:36:37,933
I won't run away, Drake.

580
00:36:38,976 --> 00:36:41,896
Not now, not today.

581
00:36:43,063 --> 00:36:44,064
Not tomorrow.

582
00:36:44,690 --> 00:36:46,358
I'm all yours this week.

583
00:36:47,495 --> 00:36:49,403
And then, what happens next?

584
00:36:51,780 --> 00:36:52,990
Drake...

585
00:36:56,285 --> 00:36:59,246
Will you please stop thinking
and just let things happen?

586
00:37:01,707 --> 00:37:05,252
Happy endings aren't always
the best part of the story.

587
00:37:09,590 --> 00:37:11,342
It's the chase.

588
00:37:12,343 --> 00:37:13,719
It's the memories.

589
00:37:14,261 --> 00:37:15,638
It's the fun!

590
00:37:19,767 --> 00:37:21,685
Those are the
best parts of the story.

591
00:37:28,651 --> 00:37:29,558
Alys?

592
00:37:29,881 --> 00:37:30,729
Hmm?

593
00:37:31,950 --> 00:37:36,413
I'm okay with you
making me chase after you.

594
00:37:36,867 --> 00:37:39,058
As long as you're my end game.

595
00:37:45,709 --> 00:37:46,835
Go eat.

596
00:37:46,835 --> 00:37:49,380
You eat.
You've barely touched anything.

597
00:37:52,800 --> 00:37:53,842
Uhm...

598
00:37:54,760 --> 00:37:55,928
Alys, can I ask you something?

599
00:37:56,387 --> 00:37:57,263
Hmm.

600
00:37:57,763 --> 00:37:59,556
What do you want to know?

601
00:38:04,144 --> 00:38:06,438
Have you ever considered
marrying me?

602
00:38:14,238 --> 00:38:15,322
Yes.

603
00:38:16,378 --> 00:38:17,866
That was the option, right?

604
00:38:18,993 --> 00:38:20,160
That was the plan—

605
00:38:20,160 --> 00:38:20,995
- Was?
- And the...

606
00:38:24,581 --> 00:38:25,374
Fine.

607
00:38:26,333 --> 00:38:27,126
Is.

608
00:38:38,804 --> 00:38:41,056
I don't know, it's really confusing.
It's so weird!

609
00:38:41,056 --> 00:38:43,267
It feels like we’re back
in high school again.

610
00:38:43,267 --> 00:38:46,937
So, how's your heart doing, Bestie?

611
00:38:47,813 --> 00:38:49,523
Don't tell me it was nothing.

612
00:38:52,067 --> 00:38:53,193
It's nothing.

613
00:38:53,861 --> 00:38:55,847
Cross your heart?

614
00:38:56,155 --> 00:38:59,241
Swear it on your dying skin cells?

615
00:39:00,576 --> 00:39:02,703
What should I be feeling?

616
00:39:02,703 --> 00:39:03,871
I don't know.

617
00:39:03,871 --> 00:39:06,040
Every time he looks at me, it's like...

618
00:39:06,707 --> 00:39:09,335
nothing ever broke.
Like nothing ever happened.

619
00:39:10,044 --> 00:39:11,086
Oh.

620
00:39:11,086 --> 00:39:12,880
So there is something.

621
00:39:16,008 --> 00:39:16,967
Fine!

622
00:39:18,218 --> 00:39:19,401
I'm mad.

623
00:39:19,720 --> 00:39:21,221
Just mad?

624
00:39:22,139 --> 00:39:23,807
I know you, Bestie.

625
00:39:26,101 --> 00:39:27,433
Fine.

626
00:39:27,811 --> 00:39:29,646
I felt a little flutter.

627
00:39:29,646 --> 00:39:31,231
Damn it.

628
00:39:31,231 --> 00:39:34,860
I don't know why do I have to
feel this way again with him.

629
00:39:36,054 --> 00:39:39,933
Bestie, he was never
gone in the first place.

630
00:39:40,074 --> 00:39:41,450
And knowing Drake,

631
00:39:41,450 --> 00:39:43,494
you know that's just how he is.

632
00:39:43,494 --> 00:39:45,037
It's Drake.

633
00:39:45,037 --> 00:39:47,831
He can't help but make
you feel things again.

634
00:39:48,874 --> 00:39:51,347
That's what I'm afraid of, Bestie.

635
00:39:52,669 --> 00:39:54,088
What if...

636
00:39:55,047 --> 00:39:57,424
What if he still wants me but

637
00:39:58,342 --> 00:39:59,802
I don't deserve him?

638
00:40:00,010 --> 00:40:01,220
Bestie...

639
00:40:01,220 --> 00:40:04,056
That's for Drake to decide, not you.

640
00:40:04,556 --> 00:40:06,058
If he wants you,

641
00:40:06,308 --> 00:40:07,601
he wants you.

642
00:40:07,601 --> 00:40:08,894
Period.

643
00:40:28,789 --> 00:40:30,082
Seriously?

644
00:40:30,374 --> 00:40:32,459
You actually slept on the couch?

645
00:40:36,839 --> 00:40:38,132
Good night, Drake.

646
00:40:49,893 --> 00:40:51,520
Good night, Drakey Baby.

647
00:41:06,326 --> 00:41:07,619
Good morning!

648
00:41:09,580 --> 00:41:10,873
Good morning!

649
00:41:16,295 --> 00:41:17,588
What's that?

650
00:41:21,133 --> 00:41:22,885
Breakfast in bed.

651
00:41:23,510 --> 00:41:26,472
Wow, it's like we're newly weds.

652
00:41:26,889 --> 00:41:28,515
It's just practice.

653
00:41:29,850 --> 00:41:30,767
Confident?

654
00:41:30,934 --> 00:41:31,751
Of course.

655
00:41:32,769 --> 00:41:35,147
I know he just ordered this,

656
00:41:35,172 --> 00:41:36,548
but it still makes me happy.

657
00:41:37,441 --> 00:41:40,527
Gestures like these would never
fail to make a girl smile.

658
00:41:40,944 --> 00:41:42,657
A timeless act, in fact.

659
00:41:45,157 --> 00:41:47,034
You've fallen for me, Alys.

660
00:41:47,993 --> 00:41:52,039
And you’ll still end up falling for me.

661
00:41:52,539 --> 00:41:53,634
It's inevitable.

662
00:41:54,541 --> 00:41:56,168
Whatever you say, Palma.

663
00:42:04,384 --> 00:42:06,470
OMG, what's this?

664
00:42:10,015 --> 00:42:11,183
Is this mine?

665
00:42:13,406 --> 00:42:15,954
Girls and their jewelries.

666
00:42:18,190 --> 00:42:19,900
Boys and their toys.

667
00:42:21,944 --> 00:42:23,278
Those are all for you.

668
00:42:24,821 --> 00:42:26,290
Are you serious?

669
00:42:37,459 --> 00:42:39,259
I never cheated on you.

670
00:42:43,298 --> 00:42:44,633
Then why are you laughing?

671
00:42:47,594 --> 00:42:48,929
I'm just grateful.

672
00:42:49,814 --> 00:42:51,932
To hold your hand again.

673
00:42:53,767 --> 00:42:55,673
To be able to speak to you.

674
00:42:57,312 --> 00:42:59,314
It feels like home, Alys.

675
00:42:59,648 --> 00:43:02,651
He's never this vocal
about his feelings for me.

676
00:43:03,193 --> 00:43:05,320
I'm not used to this but,

677
00:43:05,320 --> 00:43:07,281
it feels freaking good.

678
00:43:07,698 --> 00:43:11,827
Having him makes me thankful for
breathing and waking up every day.

679
00:43:13,370 --> 00:43:14,830
Thank you.

680
00:43:15,664 --> 00:43:17,499
What are these for?

681
00:43:22,212 --> 00:43:24,047
My gifts to you.

682
00:43:27,843 --> 00:43:29,678
This one is for your birthday.

683
00:43:31,972 --> 00:43:33,390
This one is for anniversary.

684
00:43:37,242 --> 00:43:38,666
For monthsary.

685
00:43:41,231 --> 00:43:42,899
For saying thank you.

686
00:43:45,360 --> 00:43:47,029
For saying sorry.

687
00:43:49,990 --> 00:43:51,658
And for saying I love you.

688
00:43:57,623 --> 00:44:00,042
I don't know,
I just wanted to give you a gift.

689
00:44:01,752 --> 00:44:03,128
I'm so happy

690
00:44:04,796 --> 00:44:07,341
that you are part of my life.

691
00:44:14,681 --> 00:44:16,588
Damn you, Palma!

692
00:44:24,066 --> 00:44:25,275
Yeah.

693
00:44:25,707 --> 00:44:26,958
Damn me.

694
00:46:36,448 --> 00:46:39,080
The sunset's so beautiful.

695
00:46:41,077 --> 00:46:43,038
As beautiful as you.

696
00:46:46,374 --> 00:46:49,336
He's getting better at compliments.

697
00:46:50,295 --> 00:46:51,986
I hope it stays this way.

698
00:46:54,800 --> 00:46:57,221
I hope this never ends.

699
00:46:59,054 --> 00:47:00,597
Alys.

700
00:47:00,931 --> 00:47:04,309
If I could only stop
the sun from setting,

701
00:47:04,518 --> 00:47:06,186
hold back time,

702
00:47:06,686 --> 00:47:08,244
I'd do it right now.

703
00:47:10,899 --> 00:47:13,151
Let's just think that

704
00:47:14,152 --> 00:47:17,252
we're escaping from reality somehow.

705
00:47:19,407 --> 00:47:20,951
Are you happy?

706
00:47:21,458 --> 00:47:23,210
Beyond happy.

707
00:47:24,246 --> 00:47:26,873
Everything feels so soothing and

708
00:47:27,749 --> 00:47:31,920
being with you makes me feel
like i made the right decision.

709
00:47:33,171 --> 00:47:34,381
Me too.

710
00:47:34,548 --> 00:47:35,757
Tripp was right.

711
00:47:36,258 --> 00:47:37,843
I still love Drake.

712
00:47:38,426 --> 00:47:39,803
I always did.

713
00:47:40,303 --> 00:47:41,847
I will always do.

714
00:47:42,681 --> 00:47:43,932
They were right.

715
00:47:44,432 --> 00:47:47,143
No matter what happens
when you love a person,

716
00:47:47,561 --> 00:47:48,812
you can't help it.

717
00:47:49,403 --> 00:47:51,697
That's where you'll always end up.

718
00:47:52,234 --> 00:47:54,736
I wish we were always like this.

719
00:48:50,332 --> 00:48:54,252
Seriously?
You actually slept on the couch?

720
00:48:58,465 --> 00:48:59,758
Good night, Drake.

721
00:49:13,063 --> 00:49:14,814
Good night, Drakey Baby.

722
00:50:01,980 --> 00:50:04,733
I’ve waited for this moment.

723
00:50:11,496 --> 00:50:15,250
I wish we could go back to
when we were in high school.

724
00:50:17,627 --> 00:50:19,421
But this time,

725
00:50:20,672 --> 00:50:22,799
we'll make things right.

726
00:50:27,430 --> 00:50:28,566
Alys,

727
00:50:30,890 --> 00:50:34,686
I'm really, really sorry for everything.

728
00:50:38,405 --> 00:50:42,493
I hope you can forgive me
for everything I did wrong.

729
00:50:46,948 --> 00:50:49,701
But Alys, I want you to know

730
00:50:50,285 --> 00:50:52,285
that you're the only one.

731
00:50:54,539 --> 00:50:55,730
Then.

732
00:50:56,583 --> 00:50:57,834
Now.

733
00:50:58,918 --> 00:51:00,378
And until the end.

734
00:51:00,879 --> 00:51:02,297
Only you.

735
00:51:42,045 --> 00:51:45,465
On the next episode of
Dating Alys Perez.

736
00:51:46,091 --> 00:51:47,550
If I talk to Tripp,

737
00:51:48,834 --> 00:51:51,295
do you promise to stay with me in this?

738
00:51:51,596 --> 00:51:53,056
I promise.

739
00:51:53,681 --> 00:51:54,724
Zy?

740
00:51:55,141 --> 00:51:56,019
Hmm?

741
00:51:56,976 --> 00:51:58,520
Stand by your decision, okay?

742
00:52:00,313 --> 00:52:01,523
People are hurting already.

743
00:52:02,023 --> 00:52:03,066
This is enough.

744
00:52:03,775 --> 00:52:04,818
How is she?

745
00:52:05,318 --> 00:52:06,543
Fier is pregnant.
